# Now What? — environment variables (placeholders only; real secrets never committed)
#
# HOW TO USE THIS FILE
#   Local:      copy to .env.local and fill in what you need. Nothing here is required to run
#               `npm run dev` or `npm run verify` — both work with no keys at all.
#   Production: set these in the hosting dashboard, then REDEPLOY. A deployment carries the
#               environment it was built with, so nothing you type in a dashboard reaches the
#               site that is live right now.
#
# DO NOT PASTE THIS FILE WHOLESALE INTO A HOSTING DASHBOARD. It carries a real localhost value
# for NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL, which would put "localhost" into robots.txt, every canonical tag
# and all ~60 sitemap URLs.
#
# NEVER CREATE A VARIABLE AND LEAVE THE BOX EMPTY. An empty box is not the same as an absent
# one, and several of the reads below take the first value that is PRESENT. Delete the
# variable instead. (The code now trims and falls back where it can — see lib/config.ts
# `usdFromEnv` and lib/kv/redis.ts `cred` — but leaving it out is still the safe habit.)
#
# TO CHECK YOUR WIRING: GET /api/health. It reports whether a key and a metering store were
# found, and the cost caps and model that ACTUALLY took effect. It never returns a secret.


# --- Anthropic (server-side only) ---------------------------------------------------------
# Powers every generated surface: /ask, /decode (including reading a photographed letter),
# the chat panel, and — since the Review Builder work — two steps INSIDE the main /start
# flow: the drafted application in the analysis, and the rewritten letter.
# Without it none of those break: each degrades to its deterministic output and /start still
# works end to end. It is just plainer, and /ask can never answer anything.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. A separate key for the "Work it out with us" chat panel, so its spend shows as its
# own line on the Anthropic console. Chat is the hardest surface to cost-forecast because it
# is open-ended. Leave blank and chat bills to ANTHROPIC_API_KEY like everything else.
# IT IS NOT A SUBSTITUTE FOR ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. Set only this one and the app believes a model
# is available — /api/health even reports model:true — while every surface except chat resolves
# to an empty key and quietly degrades.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_CHAT=

# Optional: override the grounded-answer model. Default: claude-sonnet-5.
# ONLY USE A MODEL LISTED IN MODEL_PRICES_USD_PER_MTOK (lib/config.ts). A model that is not in
# that table cannot be metered accurately; it now bills at the dearest price we know, which
# protects the budget but will exhaust it early. Add the model to the table instead.
# Priced today: claude-opus-5 · claude-sonnet-5 · claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=

# --- Upstash Redis (cost meter + rate limit; FAIL-CLOSED when unset in prod) ---------------
# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION. Without a metering store the cost guard cannot meter safely, so it
# denies: every model-backed route answers "Service is temporarily unavailable". The
# deterministic /start flow, deadlines, help routing and the FAQ pages keep working.
# Create the database BEFORE setting these — the tokens do not exist until it does. Put it in
# ap-southeast-2 (Sydney) to match the syd1 function region in vercel.json; the guard makes
# several sequential round trips per call, so a distant database is felt on every answer.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
# Some hosts inject the KV_* names instead (harness §15) — either pair works, per field.
# Set ONE pair. If your host injects KV_REST_API_*, do not also create empty UPSTASH_* boxes.
KV_REST_API_URL=
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=

# --- Cost guard ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Plain numbers only — no "$", no "USD". A value that is not a number falls back to the
# default rather than becoming it, so a typo here means your intended cap never took effect.
# Confirm the live values on /api/health.
# A deliberate 0 IS honoured: it is the only way to switch model spend off without a deploy.
# Per-session ceiling. Default 5.
SESSION_CAP_USD=5
# Daily kill-switch across all visitors. Default 50, which is roughly 1,400 full sessions/day.
GLOBAL_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=50
# (The per-IP ceiling — 30 requests/hour — is hardcoded in lib/config.ts, not an env var.)

# --- OCR (reading a photographed or PDF letter; in memory, never stored) -------------------
# Values: "anthropic" · "gcv" · "none".
# THE DEFAULT IS NOT "OFF". Leaving this blank means: use the vision model whenever
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set. So a blank box plus a key ships photo upload, and every upload is
# billed against the caps above. To actually disable uploads, write the word none.
# Pasting text always works regardless.
OCR_PROVIDER=
# Only read when OCR_PROVIDER=gcv (Google Cloud Vision).
OCR_API_KEY=

# --- Site ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Single source of truth for canonical/sitemap/robots/JSON-LD/share images (harness §8).
# BAKED IN AT BUILD TIME, like every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value — changing it needs a rebuild, not a
# restart, and the localhost value below must never reach production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Analytics (PII-safe; loader no-ops when unset) ----------------------------------------
# Also baked in at build time. Note the privacy policy names Google Analytics as a provider
# whether or not this is set, so a deployment without it describes a tool it does not load.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=

# --- Email (Resend): the contact form ------------------------------------------------------
# The contact form needs RESEND_API_KEY *and* an operator inbox. With only one of the two it
# stays off and the visitor is told "Messages aren't set up yet" with a link to free help.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# OPTIONAL verified sender, e.g. "Now What? <noreply@yourdomain.au>".
# Leave BLANK to use Resend's sandbox sender (onboarding@resend.dev) — no domain needed,
# but it can ONLY deliver to your own Resend account email, so set the operator inbox to
# that address. The visitor auto-acknowledgement is suppressed until a real domain is set.
CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=
# Operator inbox for contact-form messages (harness §16.3).
# On the sandbox sender this MUST be the email you signed up to Resend with.
ADMIN_NOTIFY_EMAIL=
# Legacy alias for the operator inbox (used only if ADMIN_NOTIFY_EMAIL is unset).
CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=

# --- LEAVE THIS OFF ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set to "1" and a copy of every /ask, /decode and /chat interaction — including the text of
# the letter someone pasted — is emailed to the operator inbox. While it is on, the on-page
# promise that nothing you type is kept, and the privacy policy, are both untrue.
# It exists for supervised QA on test data only. It is off unless this says exactly "1".
QA_EMAIL_INTERACTIONS=

# --- Dev conveniences (gated to non-prod) --------------------------------------------------
# DEV_FAKE_NOW=2026-06-16T00:00:00.000Z
#
# NOT AN ENV VAR, but set in the hosting project: Node >= 20, the syd1 region (vercel.json
# pins it), and Web Analytics enabled — the <Analytics/> tag reports nothing until it is.
#
# CRON_SECRET was listed here previously. Nothing reads it and no cron job is declared, so
# there is nothing for it to protect. If a scheduled reminder is ever added, it needs both a
# `crons` block in vercel.json and an explicit secret check in the route.
